  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 152 PM EST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\n- Rain chances Wednesday then turning cooler\n\nMoisture increases in southerly flow through Wednesday with height\nfalls as upper low approaches, but chances for rain remain low\nthrough Tuesday. The better chance for measurable rain is not \nuntil Wednesday and even then it looks like heavy rain is unlikely\nwith convection remaining south of the forecast area and dry\nslotting occurring rather quickly.\n\nWraparound, lake-enhanced showers, along with cooler temperatures\ncan be expected through the end of the week as upper troughing\nremains and is eventually reloaded this weekend by a vigorous \nnorthern stream shortwave trough. Current slight chance POPs for\nthe weekend may eventually trend higher given decent ensemble \nsupport got the timing and location of this trough.",
